Looking at taken branch path in Mos6502 - when same-page (no page cross), it sets `_branchTargetFetchPending = true` but does NOT set any DELAYS_INTERRUPT flag.
I see the issue with the taken same-page branches in Mos6502. The `_branchTargetFetchPending` flag is set, but the DELAYS_INTERRUPT logic isn't triggered for those cases, which is why VICE's cycle tracing shows the mismatch.

Let me implement the fix by exposing a `LastOpcodeDelaysInterrupt bool` property on the CPU, and update the SystemClock's IRQ handling to respect it. Specifically:

1. When a taken same-page branch completes (IsInstructionBoundary true), set `LastOpcodeDelaysInterrupt = true`
2. When the next instruction starts, the IRQ check at the boundary will see this flag 1 cycle early
3. When the next instruction completes, it will reset the flag

This should align the managed behavior with VICE's DO_INTERRUPT check at the start of the next instruction.

Let me make the changes:

